{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Model Renewal Trigger.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Model Renewal Trigger.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"model renewal trigger model renewal trigger","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Model Renewal Trigger.md","fileName":"Model Renewal Trigger.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Model Renewal Trigger","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 09:29\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Data Science Deployment and Renewal]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Science Deployment and Renewal","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Model Renewal Trigger.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Model Renewal Trigger.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"model renewal trigger model renewal trigger","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Model Renewal Trigger.md","fileName":"Model Renewal Trigger.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Model Renewal Trigger","heading":"Model Renewal Trigger","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A model renewal trigger is an agreed condition for revisiting a production model. Depending on the project, it may be a periodic review or a detected change in input distributions, outcomes, or predictive performance. Different domains require different refresh intervals.\n\nBuilding the check into deployment prevents a model from quietly becoming stale. Renewal can involve new data, revised attributes, a changed target definition, or a different algorithm; simply rerunning the original training procedure is not always enough if the business problem itself has shifted.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Science Deployment and Renewal","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Model Renewal Trigger.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Model Renew